1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,667
A Cart With One Wobbly Wheel.

3
00:00:03,667 --> 00:00:07,458
Our shopping cart makes a tiny squeak every time Mom turns a corner.

4
00:00:07,458 --> 00:00:09,646
Ben thinks it sounds like a mouse.

5
00:00:09,646 --> 00:00:12,583
I think it sounds like a mouse asking for a vacation.

6
00:00:12,868 --> 00:00:15,883
We need milk, eggs, bread, and cereal.

7
00:00:15,883 --> 00:00:18,122
Lucy, can you hold the list?

8
00:00:18,388 --> 00:00:19,798
And cookies.

9
00:00:19,798 --> 00:00:21,798
Very important cookies.

10
00:00:22,084 --> 00:00:23,609
Is that on the list?

11
00:00:23,609 --> 00:00:27,526
Ben looks over my shoulder as if the word might appear if he stares hard enough.

12
00:00:27,526 --> 00:00:28,807
It doesn't.

13
00:00:28,807 --> 00:00:32,088
We reach the end of the aisle, but there's still no cereal.

14
00:00:32,356 --> 00:00:33,787
Excuse me.

15
00:00:33,787 --> 00:00:35,829
Which aisle is the cereal in?

16
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,500
Aisle five, next to the oatmeal.

17
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,969
The signs above you show the aisle numbers.

18
00:00:41,236 --> 00:00:42,417
Thanks.

19
00:00:42,417 --> 00:00:46,042
In aisle five, Ben picks up the biggest box he can reach.

20
00:00:46,042 --> 00:00:48,428
It's almost the size of his backpack.

21
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,827
This one has a spaceship on it.

22
00:00:51,052 --> 00:00:53,535
Let's compare the smaller box, too.

23
00:00:53,535 --> 00:00:57,223
We only need enough for this week, and we already have some at home.

24
00:00:57,508 --> 00:01:00,720
We choose the smaller box and cross cereal off the list.

25
00:01:00,720 --> 00:01:03,335
At checkout, I count four things.

26
00:01:03,335 --> 00:01:06,356
Milk, eggs, bread, and cereal.

27
00:01:06,356 --> 00:01:07,616
Perfect.

28
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,985
The cart did all that work without getting any cookies.

29
00:01:11,212 --> 00:01:13,277
The cart doesn't eat cookies.

30
00:01:13,516 --> 00:01:15,447
That explains the squeaking.

31
00:01:15,447 --> 00:01:16,853
It's upset.

32
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:19,155
We park it with the other carts.

33
00:01:19,155 --> 00:01:20,925
I give it a little wave.

34
00:01:20,925 --> 00:01:23,259
Thanks for the ride, tiny mouse.

35
00:01:23,259 --> 00:01:24,852
Enjoy your break.
